<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">21 December in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 21 December, from 69 to 1988.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/69">69 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,957 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Senate recognises Vespasian as emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The day after Vitellius was killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, the Senate granted Vespasian the powers of emperor, ending the Year of the Four Emperors. His Flavian dynasty restored stability and began the Colosseum.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-iii-of-germany" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/conrad-iii-of-germany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1140 CE <span class="tih-ago">886 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Weinsberg surrenders to Conrad III after a siege</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a siege of several weeks, the town and castle of Weinsberg surrendered to King Conrad III, the first ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen dynasty</a>. The siege was a decisive clash in the rivalry between the Hohenstaufen and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Welfs</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/conrad-iii-of-germany">Conrad III of Germany</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1237">1237 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">789 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Batu Khan's Mongols sack Ryazan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After a short siege, the Mongol army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a> destroyed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a>, the first city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kievan-rus">Kievan Rus'</a> to be besieged in the invasion. The city never recovered, and the seat of the principality moved to Pereslavl-Ryazansky.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ryazan">Ryazan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batu-khan">Batu Khan</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1361">1361 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">665 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Castile defeats the forces of Granada at Linuesa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Huesa in the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaen">Jaén</a>, the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a> defeated those of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a>, the last independent Muslim state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-europe">Western Europe</a>, in an action of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-castile">Kingdom of Castile</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1620">1620 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">406 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A Mayflower party lands at Plymouth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">An exploring party from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mayflower">Mayflower</a> landed at Plymouth harbour, where the Pilgrims decided to settle (11 December Old Style). Half the colonists died during the first winter.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1898">1898 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">128 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Curies identify radium</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Working in a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a> shed, Marie and Pierre Curie detected a new, intensely radioactive element in pitchblende, announced days later as radium. Isolating it took Marie Curie another twelve years.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 8 launches for the Moon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Frank Borman, Jim Lovell and Bill Anders lifted off on the first crewed flight to leave Earth's orbit. On Christmas Eve they orbited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a> and photographed 'Earthrise'.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1988">1988 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">38 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">A bomb destroys Pan Am Flight 103 over Lockerbie</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A bomb exploded aboard a Boeing 747 over Lockerbie in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, killing all 259 on board and 11 people on the ground. A Libyan intelligence officer was convicted in 2001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 21 December <span class="n">7</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/masaccio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/masaccio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Masaccio</span><span class="tp">1401–1428</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/man-singh-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/man-singh-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Man Singh I</span><span class="tp">1550–1614</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/leopold-von-ranke"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/leopold-von-ranke.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Leopold von Ranke</span><span class="tp">1795–1886</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/benjamin-disraeli"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/benjamin-disraeli.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Benjamin Disraeli</span><span class="tp">1804–1881</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/william-ruto"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-ruto.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">William Ruto</span><span class="tp">b. 1966</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mikheil-saakashvili"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mikheil-saakashvili.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mikheil Saakashvili</span><span class="tp">b. 1967</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/emmanuel-macron"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/emmanuel-macron.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Emmanuel Macron</span><span class="tp">b. 1977</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 21 December <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hugh-of-tuscany"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hugh-of-tuscany.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hugh of Tuscany</span><span class="tp">c. 953–1001</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-boccaccio"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giovanni-boccaccio.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giovanni Boccaccio</span><span class="tp">1313–1375</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/peter-canisius"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/peter-canisius.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Peter Canisius</span><span class="tp">1521–1597</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-garnier"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-garnier.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis Garnier</span><span class="tp">1839–1873</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mohammed-abdullah-hassan"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mohammed-abdullah-hassan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mohammed Abdullah Hassan</span><span class="tp">1856–1920</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
